From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:34:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 18/18] wifi: b43: keep one A-MPDU in flight per
 ring

The next A-MPDU was built as soon as fewer than two were queued on the
DMA ring, so a second aggregate went out right behind the first. On
BCM4331 (5 GHz HT40, MCS 15) about twice as many MPDUs then needed
retries (10-11% vs 4-5% of transmitted MPDUs, none finally failed) and
TCP saw retransmissions, which kept its window small.

Build the next aggregate only from the TX status of the previous one.
Frames that arrive meanwhile wait in the software queue and go out in
one larger aggregate.

Measured with 20-second iperf3 runs at close range, two rounds each:
TCP TX 168-172 -> 191-192 Mbit/s and its retransmissions ~20 -> 0; TCP
RX, UDP RX and paced bidirectional traffic unchanged. UDP TX drops from
221-225 to 201-203 Mbit/s: a saturating sender now leaves the medium
idle while the host turns the status around. TCP is the common case, so
take the trade. The ping latency added under TCP TX goes from ~8 to
~10 ms.

With one aggregate in flight, a single A-MPDU status that never arrives
as such stops aggregation on the ring for good. A soak of this change
once stalled all TX that way about a minute in: mac80211 held 2097
frames for TID 0, the DMA ring was idle, and every flush timed out.
Recover: forget the aggregate once the ring has drained, and restart the
controller if frames have sat on the ring for a second without status.
Neither fired during the following two-hour soak, so the trigger is
not known.

Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
index 6e10d1bc68c4..a89aa3696c7b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
@@ -1442,15 +1442,34 @@ int b43_dma_tx_free_frames(struct b43_wldev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	return free_slots(ring) / TX_SLOTS_PER_FRAME;
 }
 
-/* Frames for an A-MPDU wait in the software queue while the ring already
- * has enough aggregates queued: otherwise each one goes out on its own.
+/* Frames for an A-MPDU wait in the software queue while an aggregate is
+ * still in flight: otherwise each one goes out on its own. With a second
+ * aggregate queued behind the first, about twice as many MPDUs needed
+ * retries and TCP saw retransmissions, so build the next aggregate only
+ * from the status of the previous one.
  */
-#define B43_AMPDU_INFLIGHT	2
+#define B43_AMPDU_INFLIGHT	1
 
 bool b43_dma_ampdu_busy(struct b43_wldev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
-	return select_ring_by_priority(dev, b43_tx_queue_mapping(dev, skb))->
-		ampdu_inflight >= B43_AMPDU_INFLIGHT;
+	struct b43_dmaring *ring;
+
+	ring = select_ring_by_priority(dev, b43_tx_queue_mapping(dev, skb));
+	/* Aggregation on the ring waits for the status of the A-MPDU in
+	 * flight. Should that never come back, recover instead of stalling
+	 * all traffic for good: with the ring drained the status was lost
+	 * or taken as a non-A-MPDU one; with frames still on the ring after
+	 * a second the hardware has stopped reporting, so restart it.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(ring->ampdu_inflight && !ring->used_slots)) {
+		b43dbg(dev->wl, "A-MPDU status lost on ring %d\n", ring->index);
+		ring->ampdu_inflight = 0;
+	} else if (unlikely(ring->ampdu_inflight &&
+			    time_after(jiffies, ring->ampdu_stamp + HZ))) {
+		ring->ampdu_stamp = jiffies;
+		b43_controller_restart(dev, "A-MPDU status timeout");
+	}
+	return ring->ampdu_inflight >= B43_AMPDU_INFLIGHT;
 }
 
 /* Queue the MPDUs of one A-MPDU (all to the same TID and peer, at the same
@@ -1501,6 +1520,7 @@ int b43_dma_tx_ampdu(struct b43_wldev *dev, struct sk_buff_head *list,
 	}
 
 	ring->ampdu_inflight++;
+	ring->ampdu_stamp = jiffies;
 	if (free_slots(ring) < TX_SLOTS_PER_FRAME) {
 		b43_stop_queue(dev, queue);
 		dev->wl->tx_queue_stopped[queue] = true;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
index 618c76e0ac6e..c7b2d27dd0d4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.h
@@ -263,6 +263,8 @@ struct b43_dmaring {
 	bool stopped;
 	/* A-MPDUs queued and not yet reported */
 	int ampdu_inflight;
+	/* When the last A-MPDU was handed to the hardware */
+	unsigned long ampdu_stamp;
 	/* The QOS priority assigned to this ring. Only used for TX rings.
 	 * This is the mac80211 "queue" value. */
 	u8 queue_prio;
